Keeps a color's alpha unrounded in Color::toArray. It rounded alpha to two
decimal places, so to-rgba, Color::serialize, and the style property getters
read #ff000080's alpha 0.502 as 0.5, and a color read and set again changed.
GL JS's to-rgba returns alpha as is. Color::stringify, which backs to-string
and style JSON, now matches GL JS's Color.toString: whole channels and alpha as
is. Before, it wrote unrounded channels and rounded alpha.
(https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native-ffi/issues/1707)
Upstream: not proposed

